# clasp push allowlist for leader-hub's single Apps Script project
# (Code.gs + EmailBridge.gs, serving both the HTML web app and the JSON
# API — see Code.gs's own header comment for the server-migration plan
# these are phase 1 of; plus AiPrompts.gs, which holds the six AI-flow
# system prompts EmailBridge.gs's queue hands to the Flows). Everything else here — the LEADERHUB_*/LH_0*
# docs and drive-tools/ (one-off paste-and-run admin utilities, never a
# persistent deployment — see drive-tools/LH_Drive_README.md) — must
# never reach the live script. student-leader-hub.html DOES now need to
# reach the live script (Code.gs's doGet() serves it via
# HtmlService.createHtmlOutputFromFile) — it stays the generated,
# never-hand-edited file tools/leaderhub-build/build.js produces; only
# its allowlist status here changed, not how it's built. Allowlist
# style, same rationale as kos-personal/.claspignore: safer against
# future additions than a denylist that has to be kept in sync by hand.
**/**

!appsscript.json
!EmailBridge.gs
!Code.gs
!Config.gs
!Data.gs
!SCR.gs
!AiPrompts.gs
!student-leader-hub.html
